{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on the cutover deployment: no deployment tonight. It runs\nafter three things: CDF-1 on main, a reviewed plan note, and your\nanswer to the question at the end of this act.\n\nWhy. I prepared the runbook tonight, read only. The deployment is\nnot one run of `deploy.mjs`:\n- Each Worker needs a new register. `dap install --plan` signs a\n  plan that lives 840 s, and the Worker accepts the install only for\n  the register that `REGISTER_SCOPE` names. So plan, pin, deploy and\n  install fall in one window of 14 minutes for each Worker.\n- `deploy.mjs` takes no override, and a tracked setting changes only\n  in a reviewed head. No head lands in 14 minutes.\n- On a register of policy `keys`, `dap create` must follow the\n  install in 900 s, or the register never founds a room.\n\nThe plan, which the note will hold for the checker's review:\n1. Window: for each Worker, a direct Wrangler deployment of the\n   tracked file at main, with `--var` for the register settings\n   only, as `docs/deploy.md` allows for reviewed overrides. Then the\n   install and one bare room. Order: lending, grow, demo,\n   artroom-scope, connect, sandbox.\n2. Head A: the tracked files take the same register values. Then\n   `deploy.mjs` deploys with receipts again.\n3. A release head: the new Grow and Lending releases from canonical\n   sources. Head B: trust rows and the Lending content bucket.\n4. The Grow, Lending and J5 Site rooms. Head C: the screen hosts.\n\nRequests follow for head A and for the release head. The runbook\nand the room inventory are in\n~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-cutover-deployment-prep.\n\nQuestion for you, before the window. `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` names the\nold Grow directory until AE-1. After the deployment that directory\nis retired. What does the archive driver of the Grow Worker do on\neach alarm then: does it stop with a named result, retry without\nend, or throw? Read the source and answer in one act. Run nothing.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}